---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/ui/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/ui/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — FindSongKey"
  description="Read FindSongKey's privacy policy. Learn how we handle your data — all audio analysis happens in your browser. No files are uploaded to our servers."
  canonical="https://findsongkeybpm.com/privacy-policy"
>
  <Header />
  <main class="content-page" id="privacy-policy">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="content-meta">Last updated: June 4, 2026</p>

    <p>
      At FindSongKey, your privacy is fundamental to how we build our product. This
      Privacy Policy explains what data we collect, how we use it, and your rights
      regarding that data. By using our website, you agree to the terms outlined below.
    </p>

    <h2>1. No audio data collection</h2>
    <p>
      All audio analysis — including BPM detection, key detection, and Camelot wheel
      mapping — happens entirely within your web browser using WebAssembly (WASM)
      technology. Your audio files are <strong>never uploaded</strong> to our servers.
      They remain on your device from start to finish. We do not store, process, or
      have access to any audio files you analyze.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
    <p>
      While we don't collect audio data, we may collect limited information to
      improve our service:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Usage analytics</strong> — Anonymous page views, session duration,
        and general interaction patterns to help us understand how users engage with
        our tool.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Device information</strong> — Browser type, operating system, screen
        resolution, and language preference. This helps us optimize compatibility
        across devices.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Error logs</strong> — If the tool encounters an error, we may
        collect anonymized diagnostic data to fix bugs and improve reliability.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Cookies and local storage</h2>
    <p>
      We use minimal cookies and browser local storage for functionality purposes:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Theme preference</strong> — We store your light/dark mode choice in
        local storage so it persists between visits.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Advertising cookies</strong> — Our advertising partners (Google
        AdSense) may use cookies to serve relevant ads. You can manage these
        preferences through your browser settings or Google's ad personalization
        controls.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Third-party services</h2>
    <p>We use the following third-party services:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Google AdSense</strong> — To display advertisements that help keep
        FindSongKey free. Google may use cookies to serve personalized ads based on
        your browsing history. Learn more at
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="content-link">
          Google's Privacy Policy</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Cloudflare</strong> — For website hosting and performance
        optimization. Cloudflare may collect limited technical data as described in
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="content-link">
          Cloudflare's Privacy Policy</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Data retention</h2>
    <p>
      Since we don't collect audio data or personal information, there is minimal
      data to retain. Any anonymized analytics data is aggregated and cannot be
      traced back to individual users. Advertising cookies are managed by third-party
      providers according to their own retention policies.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
      FindSongKey is not directed at children under the age of 13. We do not
      knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child
      has provided us with personal data, please contact us so we can take
      appropriate action.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Access any personal data we hold about you</li>
      <li>Request deletion of your data</li>
      <li>Opt out of personalized advertising</li>
      <li>Withdraw consent for data processing</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To exercise any of these rights, please contact us at the email address
      provided on our <a href="/contact" class="content-link">Contact page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be
      posted on this page with an updated revision date. We encourage you to review
      this policy periodically to stay informed about how we protect your privacy.
    </p>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
